  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the task, tooling notes, and installed OpenSocrates controller, then collect and reconcile the source files before building the analysis and board materials.\n",
    "I’m using the installed OpenSocrates controller for the recommendation and evidence judgments. The financial model will use the frozen source-room data, with synthetic client inputs clearly separated from archived public observations.\n",
    "The archive includes replacement order revisions, duplicate extract rows, an orphan return, and returns on both sides of the cutoff. I’ll keep an order-level audit trail so the monthly totals and hub scenarios can be traced to the retained records.\n",
    "The reconciled 2025 base is 1,254 shipped orders, €4.384 million net sales, and €2.030 million contribution. Czechia plus Spain leads the base scenario at about €198,099 incremental annual contribution for €225,000 capex and five FTE. Netherlands plus Spain performs better under the specified return/FX stress; I’m quantifying that trade-off and the assumptions that would change the choice.\n",
    "A material assumption needs validation: every hub’s proposed saving per unit exceeds the country’s recorded fulfillment cost per unit. I’ll retain the required client scenarios and add a sensitivity that caps savings at that recorded cost. This supports staging the investment, with Spain first and explicit demand, savings, and FX gates for Czechia.\n",
    "The workbook now links the order ledger, monthly and country totals, scenarios, and portfolio comparisons through formulas. It includes all 15 pairs, with four flagged as infeasible. I’m building the report and deck around the key trade-off: Czechia plus Spain leads the normal volume cases; Netherlands plus Spain offers stronger downside performance.\n",
    "The 12-page report and 10-slide board deck are generated, and their rendered pages are legible. I’m now independently rebuilding the totals from raw inputs, checking workbook formulas and cached values, and reviewing the cutoff, correction, zero-price, and orphan-return cases. The recommendation remains conditional on demand, savings, site costs, and cash requirements that the sources do not establish.\n",
    "The independent reconstruction agrees with every monthly result and required scenario. The package has passed 718 checks, and an offline rebuild reproduced `metrics.json` byte for byte. All 22 PDF pages rendered without text outside the page. The remaining verification limit is native Excel rendering and recalculation: I checked the workbook’s formulas, caches, links, and browser preview, but no Excel or LibreOffice engine is installed.\n",
    "Completed the [full handover package](deliverables/meridian_handover.zip), including saved evidence, scripts and reproduction instructions.\n\n- [Executive report](deliverables/meridian_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](deliverables/meridian_board.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](deliverables/meridian_analysis.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](deliverables/metrics.json)\n\nRecommendation: stage **Czechia + Spain**, requiring **€225,000 capex and five FTE**, with **€198,099 base annual incremental contribution**. Start with Spain; gate Czechia on demand, savings and FX validation.\n\nPassed 718 checks and rendered all 22 PDF pages. Financial JSON reproduced identically. Native Excel recalculation remains unverified; material limitations are documented.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: evidence-hierarchy@3, trade-off-analysis@3, sensitivity-analysis@3"
  ],
